WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
Look down almost any street.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.810
One set of power lines,

3
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.510
one set of water pipes.

4
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:09.560
That same street may have three
coffee shops and two gas stations,

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.390
all fighting for customers.

6
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.840
Yet no rival ever digs up the road to lay

7
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.590
a second set of pipes.

8
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.900
So why might it make sense for only one

9
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.400
company to lay the lines and pipes?

10
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.240
In this mission, you'll draw
the natural monopoly graph

11
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.390
and find the socially optimal
price and the fair-return price.

12
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.030
Then you'll play regulator,
set a price cap in a graph lab,

13
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.840
and see what the firm does.

14
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.330
Your mission: explain when
one network makes sense,

15
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.190
and how to stop it overcharging.
